            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 63-year-old male, admitted on 03/10/1973 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with guarding. Laboratory investigations confirmed leukocytosis consistent with an acute inflammatory process. Abdominal ultrasonography supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. Given the clinical and diagnostic findings, the patient underwent laparoscopic appendectomy without intraoperative complications. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided, pain was managed adequately, and the patient was mobilized early with physiotherapy support. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. The patient was discharged home in good general condition on 07/10/1973. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks for wound inspection and general recovery assessment. Yours sincerely.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
